## ⚠️ **Critical: Always Run Commands in Theme Directory**
All npm commands (`npm run dev`, `npm run start:assets`, etc.) must run in:
```
wp-content/themes/chairforce/
```
**NOT** in the repository root!

## ⚠️ **PHP & WP-CLI — use DDEV (not the host shell)**

This project runs in **DDEV** (`chairforce-2026`, https://chairforce-2026.test).
Host `php` and `wp` are **not** wired to WordPress — always use DDEV from the
**repository root**:

```bash
cd /path/to/chairforce-2026   # repo root — NOT wp-content/themes/chairforce/

# WP-CLI (options, posts, meta, eval, db queries, etc.)
ddev wp option get woocommerce_enable_reviews
ddev wp post meta get <product_id> parts --format=json
ddev wp eval 'echo get_bloginfo("name");'

# PHP one-offs inside the web container (same PHP/WP as the site)
ddev exec php -r 'require "wp-load.php"; echo get_option("siteurl");'
ddev php path/to/script.php   # if the script expects wp-load.php

# Interactive shell in the web container
ddev ssh
```

**When to use which:**
- **Theme builds** (`npm run build`, etc.) → theme directory on the host (see above).
- **WordPress/PHP inspection, migrations, WP-CLI** → `ddev wp` / `ddev exec php` from repo root.

Do not report “WP-CLI unavailable” without trying `ddev wp` first.

**Note:** The legacy live/reference site may be a separate DDEV project
(`chairforce`, not `chairforce-2026`) — this repo’s DDEV is the rebuild workspace.

## Key Theme Concepts

- **Dual Block System**: ACF (quick setup) + JSX (preferred approach)
- **Namespace**: `Chairforce\` for all PHP classes
- **Auto-discovery**: Blocks, classes, and assets auto-register
- **WordPress Standards**: Leverages core blocks and FSE
- **Modern Workflow**: wp-scripts, Sass, browser-sync
